  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\n\nThe severe threat will continue to decrease this evening as the main\nforcing moves off to the east and convection becomes more scattered.\nCan't rule out brief heavy rainfall due to the moist environment but\nin general, hazardous weather will continue to decrease this \nevening.\n \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2)\nLow amplitude short wave will push a cold front into the area late\ntonight. Due to the orientation of the front from north-northeast to\nsouth-southwest it will be slow to move through the region. The\npotential for showers and storms will persist until this front \nclears. Some CAM solutions show better focus for storms across \nthe southern counties late tonight into Monday morning. \n\nPattern changes as broad long wave trough will move into the Great \nLakes toward mid week. This will push another cold front through the\nregion Wednesday night. Expect a change in air mass with highs \nin the 70s and lows in the 50s to lower 60s for Thursday and Friday.",
